Will you explain how "level 4" would be of relevance WRT exploding
chests? That value is quite arbitrary.

Traps on boxes and chests occur with a plain 10% probability.

The success of an #untrap is primarily (and randomly) depending on
dexterity, XL, and level difficulty; inspect the formula below...

    ch = ACURR(A_DEX) + u.ulevel;
    if (Role_if(PM_ROGUE)) ch *= 2;
    if(!force && (confused || Fumbling ||
       rnd(75+level_difficulty()/2) > ch)) {
           (void) chest_trap(otmp, FINGER, TRUE);

Examples for the rnd() arguments depending on dungeon level:
    dlvl        1   4   10   26   50
    rnd(arg)   75  77   80   88  100
When you reach the castle you may have gained, say, 12 XL and some
dexterity which would typically (over)compensate the level factor.
The success rate is quite balanced with the stats that you build up
for your character as you gain levels and descend deeper.

Whether you try to #untrap containers and failed or whether you
haven't even tried #untrap'ing, the resulting effects and their
probability are random, heavily depending on your _luck_.
A first luck check to see whether the trap makes no damage
    (Luck > -13 && rn2(13+Luck) > 7)
Then a random check whether luck will be considered at all when
determining any bad effects
    rn2(20)    i.e. unconditionally setting off trap probability 5%
               probability of exploding chest (in this case) 20%
               resulting overall probability 1%
Otherwise (with 95% probability) luck is included in the calculation,
    (Luck >= 13) ? 0 : rn2(13-Luck)
and with sufficiently luck you will not encounter exploding containers
at all (you would need a luck of -9 or less that to become possible).

